Say where a solid classifier aims its next segment from.

What it adds
  BRepClass3d_SolidExplorer aims each point's ray at a point of a face,
  taken from a parameter along one of the face's edges (myParamOnEdge).
  OtherSegment puts the parameter back after every face it tries, and
  moves it only when a point has found no face of the solid to aim at;
  the same pass is the only one that replaces a face's intersector. So
  the parameter is the one thing a classification leaves for the next,
  and while it has not moved, the points classified so far would have
  had the same answers in any order, or from another explorer of the
  same solid.

  AimParameter() returns it. Nothing in OCCT reads it. parcad classifies
  the points of one solid in runs on separate threads, each run with an
  explorer of its own, and keeps the answers only if no run's parameter
  moved; otherwise it classifies them in one run, as before.

How it was measured
  See vendor/occt-sys/PARCAD-CHANGES.md: the replies of two parts and
  the corpus, with the runs side by side and in one.

Upstream status
  Not yet reported.

